# Directory Responsibilities

| Directory | Purpose | Does NOT contain |
|-----------|---------|-----------------|
| `app/` | Pages, layouts, route handlers | Business logic, reusable components |
| `components/` | Reusable React components | Data fetching, Supabase imports |
| `lib/` | Utilities, external integrations | React components, JSX |
| `data/` | Static content/config exports | Runtime logic, API calls |
| `types/` | TypeScript interfaces only | Runtime code |
| `hooks/` | Custom React hooks | — |
| `public/` | Static assets | — |
| `supabase/` | Migrations, seed data | Application code |

# Server/Client Boundaries

- Default: Server Components.
- `"use client"` only for: event handlers, useState, useEffect, browser APIs, motion animations.
- Server-only: Supabase access, env vars (non-NEXT_PUBLIC_), cookies, headers.

# Next.js 16 Conventions

- Use `PageProps<"/route">` and `LayoutProps<"/route">` (globally available, no import needed).
- `params` is a Promise — always `await props.params`.
- Route handlers use standard Web `Request`/`Response` APIs.
- Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for API details when unsure.

# Data Flow

```
UI (components/) → Page (app/) → lib/ modules → External services (Supabase, APIs)
```

Presentational components receive data via props. They never import from `lib/supabase/`.

# Route Structure

```
/               → app/(marketing)/page.tsx
/about          → app/(marketing)/about/page.tsx
/work           → app/(marketing)/work/page.tsx
/work/[slug]    → app/(marketing)/work/[slug]/page.tsx
/services       → app/(marketing)/services/page.tsx
/contact        → app/(marketing)/contact/page.tsx
/api/health     → app/api/health/route.ts
```

# Adding New Routes

Place new marketing pages in `app/(marketing)/`. The route group provides the shared layout (navigation + footer) without affecting URLs.
